:"B.Com graduates can pursue finance roles in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public-sector banks"},{"text":"Government financial institutions"},{"text":"Public-sector enterprises"},{"text":"Treasury departments"},{"text":"Government accounting"},{"text":"Tax-related departments"},{"text":"Financial regulatory organisations"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Budgeting and audit functions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Government recruitment is post-specific, and some positions require particular examinations, professional qualifications or experience."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree is not mandatory for an entry-level Financial Analyst."},{"type":"p","text":"However, it can be valuable for specialised finance careers."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant Options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Com"},{"text":"MBA Finance"},{"text":"MBA Business Analytics"},{"text":"M.Sc Finance"},{"text":"M.Sc Financial Analytics"},{"text":"M.Sc Economics"},{"text":"PG Diploma in Financial Analysis"},{"text":"PG Diploma in Investment Banking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Route"},{"type":"p","text":"For investment-focused careers:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com","CFA","Investment Analyst / Equity Research"]},{"type":"p","text":"For corporate finance:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com","Financial Analyst","MBA Finance / CMA / relevant experience"]},{"type":"p","text":"For accounting/audit:"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Com → CA / ACCA / CMA"}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"🇺🇸 USA"},{"text":"🇬🇧 UK"},{"text":"🇨🇦 Canada"},{"text":"🇦🇺 Australia"},{"text":"🇸🇬 Singapore"},{"text":"🇩🇪 Germany"},{"text":"🇳🇱 Netherlands"},{"text":"🇫🇷 France"},{"text":"🇮🇪 Ireland"},{"text":"🇨🇭 Switzerland"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant master's:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Finance"},{"text":"Financial Economics"},{"text":"Fi